checks_run:
Built my own harness and generators, not the author's corpus. h.mjs masks through sanitizeSnapshot at every head with the same key. gen.mjs has 48 real-world templates:
- URLs with userinfo for 28 drivers, Go DSNs for 7 networks plus @/ and @(, Oracle EZConnect;
- Authorization headers in every case, Basic base64, JWTs, header blocks, Cookie and Set-Cookie;
- ini, yaml, .env, properties, toml, XML <add>, wsse tags, HTML inputs quoted and unquoted, minified HTML/CSS, meta, a .NET connectionString;
- JSON text, escaped JSON, HTML-entity JSON, CLI flags, mysql -p, env-var CLIs, SQL, form bodies, percent-encoded JSON and queries, PEM and PGP.
Secrets come in 11 styles, holding ':', '@', '/', '<', '>', quotes, backslashes, spaces and URL-safe symbols. They are checked as alphanumeric fragments, so a partial leak counts.

Differential text fuzz at 4033285 against all four earlier heads: 1,532,142 cases.
- mix: seeds 1, 11 and 12 (587k);
- boundary: element, DSN, scheme, URL and JWT glued, seed 21 (299k);
- grammar: token-level fuzz of every text rule, seeds 31 and 32 (526k);
- long: secret elements with long JWT, DSN, URL or token attributes, seeds 41 and 42 (120k).
Analysis is in regress/out-classes.txt and out-summary.txt.
- Truncation-shift cases (shown at head only because earlier masking now shortens the text) are kept apart as 'cut', not counted as masking regressions.
- All 1,138 cases that only 2ec0bba masked are short digit-free scheme values: the accepted prose design since 7193877.

findings.fix:
Read every text rule on the original text and replace the union of what they hide. Spans that overlap merge into one digest. Read the element rule twice: on the text as is, and on a copy with the other rules' spans blanked to same-length runs, so offsets still line up. Drop the 1,024 bound (`/<[\w:.-]{1,64}\s[^<>]*>/g` is still linear, since each attempt stops at the next '<').

This is regress/vfix/lib/data-diff.mjs:
- it masks E1, E2 and E3, and findings 2 and 4's shapes too;
- it passes 75/75 data-diff and corpus tests;
- 774,872 differential fuzz cases give 0 regressions against 4033285 and 4ed6449;
- CPU is about the same as head.

A smaller alternative: keep the order, drop the tag bound, and run the element rule again after DSN and JWT (fixes E1 and E2). Then also take the DSN spans from the original text (fixes E3).

Add e1_jwt_attr, e2_dsn_lt, e3_unquoted and e3_slash to the corpus.

